    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Tokyo\nNovember 29, 1948\nDearest Debby,\nWe have so enjoyed Slim's little\nbook which you so kindly sent us, and I\nagree with you that it is certainly very\nTine,\nand we are so glad to have this in\nour library.\nYour letter came some time\nahead of the book, so I waited to write you\nafter I had had a\nchance to read it. As\nyou know, I. have always been a great ad-\nmirer of\nSlim's, and it was nice to have him\nout here last January on that short visit he\nmade. I thought he looked very much the\nsame as he did in the Australia days. I\ngathered thought that his mother is far from\nwell. I certainly remember her so happily\non that trip we made across the Atlantic to-\ngether, and I always regretted that i never\nsaw her again. Have you forgotten that she\nand I were going to visit you once in St.\nLouis?\nThis must have been about 1929 or\n1930.\nIt is always a great pleasure to\nhear from you and Harold and the family, and\nwhat a delight your grandchildren must be to\nyou both! I can well picture the Christmas\n\"festivities\" when you all get together! We\nare well, the three of us. Arthur is grow-\ning to be a big boy now. He will soon be as\ntall as I am. The General is just as busy\nas ever, ana he joins me in the best of\nwishes to you and Harold ion the christmas\nseason, and a heart full of love to you both\nfrom me.\nDevotedly,",
      "Mrs. Douglas MacArthur\nAPO 500, c/o Postmaster\nSan Francisco, California OsTA.,\nNO! 30\n500\n4. P\nRVICE\nAIR MAIL\nU.S.POSTAGE\nMrs. Harold Bixby\n27 East Sixty-second Street\nNew York 21\nNew York"
    ],
